  "vendor_website": "novus.com.br",
  "description": "Universal process indicator with up to four alarms, analog retransmission and optional RS485 Modbus RTU: process value, min/max, status, alarms, input and retransmission settings, custom linearization",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-10-31",
  "firmware": "Communication manual for software V2.3x",
  "source": "Novus N1500 / N1500LC / N1500G communication manual V2.3x D (Portuguese)",
  "sources": [
    {"title": "Indicador N1500 / N1500LC / N1500G - Manual de Comunicação", "version": "V2.3x D", "url": "https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34218945/N1500_Manual_Comunicacao_PT.pdf", "note": "linked in issue #94; tables 01 and 02"}
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU needs the optional RS485 interface. Functions 03, 05 and 06; writes with address 0 are broadcast.",
    "8 data bits, 1 stop bit, no parity or even parity (chosen together with the baud rate in register 42). The manual does not give the factory address or baud rate: check the adres and bavd screens on the indicator.",
    "Every register is a signed 16-bit value. Registers 12 and up can be read and written; most registers below 12 are read-only.",
    "The process value, limits, alarm setpoints, offset and hysteresis are integers in the indicator's display unit, with the decimal places set in register 11 (dppos): 1234 with dppos = 1 is 123.4.",
    "A write outside the allowed range is not refused: the indicator stores the maximum allowed value and returns it.",
    "The F key and digital input function lists and the input type list differ on the LC model; the tables in this map are those of the standard model, and the LC values are in the register descriptions.",
    "The custom linearization points (registers 61 to 90 for the input, 91 to 120 for the indication) are not listed.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
